This function uses a recursive approach to calculate the Jacobsthal number. It handles the base cases where the position `n` is either 0 or 1, returning 0 or 1 respectively. For other positions, it uses the formula `2 * jacobsthal_num(n - 1) + jacobsthal_num(n - 2)` to calculate the next number in the sequence.

