The function `lbs` takes an array `a` as input and finds the longest bitonic subsequence. It uses two arrays `increasing` and `decreasing` of the same length to keep track of the longest increasing and decreasing subsequence in reverse order, respectively. The function then iterates through the array and updates these arrays accordingly. Finally, it calculates the length of the longest bitonic subsequence as the sum of the longest increasing and decreasing subsequences at each index, subtracting 1 to exclude the element itself from the sequence. The maximum of these lengths gives the length of the longest bitonic subsequence.

