The function `min_cost` initializes a matrix `dp` with the same dimensions as the cost matrix and fills it with infinite values. It sets the first cell `dp[0][0]` to the cost of the starting position. For other cells, it calculates the minimum cost to reach them by adding the cost of the current cell to the minimum cost of the cell above it or to the left of it. Finally, the function returns the minimum cost to reach the desired position `(m, n)`.

