In this solution, we rearrange the elements in the array such that all elements with value 0 come first, followed by all elements with value 1, and finally all elements with value 2. The "l" pointer points to the first occurrence of 1, and the "h" pointer points to the last occurrence of 2. The array is then traversed, and when an element with value 1 is encountered, it is swapped with the element pointed by the "l" pointer, increasing the "l" pointer. If an element with value 2 is encountered, it is swapped with the element pointed by the "h" pointer, decreasing the "h" pointer. This effectively segregates the elements with values 0, 1, and 2.

